SWEET AMP DSP bursts (patch 0170, plan A9f), on top of 0169 (boot-arg sweetaoc=6 + sweetamp=1): run a9e stopped at the 2880-byte XM packed
wmfw region #3 after the 72- and 528-byte regions wrote and read back on SPI13; the log did not say whether the SPI burst or the read-back
failed. sweet_amp_dsp.h: every region / .bin block is written and read back in CS-held bursts of <= 480 bytes (whole packed XM/YM/PM groups;
address = region register + byte offset, stride 4); the same bytes go to the same registers as the single burst. A failed region now prints
"SWEET AMP DSP: L|R <stage>#<n> spi-write|spi-read timeout(1)|error(2) burst +off/len" or "... read-back mismatch +off/len exp W got W",
and the stopped line tags the stage /spi-w, /spi-r or /rb. Nothing else written to the amps changes; PWR_CTRL1 stays refused. No Linux code
copied. Host test shim/amp_xnu_host_test.c (chunk boundaries vs the single-burst image, mismatch / SPI-error lines). BUILT, UNRUN.

